          "explanation": "Bishop Étienne Tempier's 1277 condemnation targeted a large list of philosophical positions, especially those associated with radical readings of Aristotle and his Arabic commentators (notably Averroes), including claims about the world's eternity and forms of necessitarianism that seemed to limit divine freedom. It shows the Aristotle controversy was an active, high-stakes institutional conflict, not a settled academic footnote.",
