          "explanation": "Falsafa coexisted and often contended with kalam (rational theology), fiqh (jurisprudence), and Sufi mysticism. It was seriously challenged from within Islamic intellectual life, most famously by Al-Ghazali's Tahafut al-Falasifa, which directly targeted Al-Farabi and Avicenna's positions.",
