        {
          "type": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Synthesis, Unraveling From Within",
          "content": "Ockham's career is best understood as a critique launched from inside the very tradition he was trained in — a Franciscan friar and Scholastic logician using the tools of Scholasticism itself (rigorous logical analysis, careful distinctions) to argue that Scholasticism's own confidence in what reason could demonstrate had overreached.\n\nWhere Aquinas built a synthesis integrating Aristotle, revelation, and natural law into one coherent structure, Ockham cut pieces of that structure away: universals as real entities, gone; confident philosophical demonstration of many theological truths, sharply limited; even, eventually, unquestioned papal political authority, challenged. His razor became a permanent tool of rigorous thought precisely because it demands justification for every theoretical commitment — including, ultimately, commitments the Scholastic tradition itself had grown comfortable making. The next and final lesson steps back to see how this entire arc — from Cicero through Aquinas to Ockham — forms one long, connected story.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"28\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Critique From Within</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"160\" width=\"900\" height=\"180\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Aquinas: builds the synthesis</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">reason + revelation, integrated</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"430\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">↓ same Scholastic tools, turned inward</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"490\" width=\"900\" height=\"180\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"550\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ockham: cuts pieces away</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">universals, demonstration, papal power</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"800\" font-size=\"21\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Next: the whole 1,700-year arc, seen together</text></svg>",
            "caption": "Ockham used the Scholastic tradition's own tools to critique its overreach."
          }
        }
